    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2022_bionlp-1_9_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "3116 chemical-disease interactions. MeSH ontology, a subset of UMLS is used to annotate entities. We follow most recent work ( Angell et al. , 2021 ; Varma et al. , 2021 ) for data pre-processing. NCBI ( Dogan et al. , 2014 ) The dataset is built from 793 PubMed abstracts. It consists of 6892 annotated disease mentions of 790 unique disease concepts. The annotators label all the mentions to concepts in MEDIC ontology ( Davis et al. , 2012 ). MEDIC is a medical dictionary that merges the diseases" .

