    kg:docId "2302.07257_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2302_07257_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "in the eld have shifted towards Vision-Language Pretraining (VLP) and utilizing pre-trained models. CLIP [ 21 ] merges visual and language information into a shared feature space, setting new state-of-the-art performance on various downstream tasks. Frozen [ 27 ] ne-tunes an image encoder, whose outputs serve as soft prompts for the language model. Flamingo [ 1 ] introduces cross-attention layers into the LLM to incorporate visual features, pre-training these new layers on billions of image-text" .

