    kg:textSpan "that outperforms prior state-of-the-art models in zero-, one-, and few-shot settings [53]. Pathways Language Model (PaLM), a dense decoder-only Transformer model, has 540 billion parameters and is trained with the pathways system. It achieved state-of-the-art few-shot performance across most tasks, with significant margins in many cases [54]. Additionally, BigScience Large Open-science Open-access Multilingual Language Model (BLOOM) is another transformer-based large language model, which is tra" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2303_11032_rag__chunk_006> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2303.11032_rag::chunk_006" ;
    kg:docId "2303.11032_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2303_11032_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "a valuable tool in NLP [61]. In general, prompt engineering leads to a new paradigm in NLP. The advanced capabilities of prompts highlight the importance of engineering them to provide values beyond simple text or code generation. However, finding the most appropriate prompt presents a new challenge. Currently, prompts can be either created manually [62, 63] or learned automatically [60, 64]. While automatically learned prompts can yield better performance in some tasks, they are often not human" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2303_11032_rag__chunk_017> a kg:Chunk ;
