    kg:textSpan "extend to multiple downstream tasks using minimally labeled natural language supervision, while leveraging largescale multi-procedural surgical videos, will be instrumental in scaling up the approaches for widespread adoption. Recent progress in surgical computer vision has started to pave the way for a new wave of AI-assisted support systems for the operating room (OR) ( Maier-Hein et al. , 2017 , 2022 ; Ward et al. , 2021 ; Mascagni et al. , 2022 ; Madani et al. , 2020 ; Yuan et al. , 2021 ). " .

