        "2212.13138_rag::chunk_003"^^xsd:string,
        "2212.13138_rag::chunk_004"^^xsd:string,
        "2212.13138_rag::chunk_013"^^xsd:string,
        "2303.11032_rag::chunk_002"^^xsd:string,
        "2303.11032_rag::chunk_005"^^xsd:string,
        "2303.11032_rag::chunk_020"^^xsd:string,
        "2304.09667_rag::chunk_010"^^xsd:string,
        "2305.09617_rag::chunk_002"^^xsd:string,
        "2305.15964_rag::chunk_001"^^xsd:string,
        "2305.15964_rag::chunk_002"^^xsd:string,
        "2305.15964_rag::chunk_003"^^xsd:string,
        "2305.15964_rag::chunk_004"^^xsd:string,
        "2309.11295_rag::chunk_002"^^xsd:string,
        "2309.11295_rag::chunk_005"^^xsd:string,
        "2309.11295_rag::chunk_007"^^xsd:string,
        "2311.06025_rag::chunk_003"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "By using a large language model, organizations, including healthcare systems, can quickly process large amounts of text data, de-identify medical records"^^xsd:string,
        "Clinical Prediction with Large Language Models (CPLLM). This method involves fine-tuning a LLM using prompts"^^xsd:string,
        "CoT prompting can elicit reasoning abilities in suciently large language models"^^xsd:string,
        "LLMs are foundation models [ 10 ], large pre-trained AI systems that can be repurposed with minimal eort across numerous domains and diverse tasks."^^xsd:string,
        "LLMs can process text data at high speed, making them an efficient tool for de-identification tasks."^^xsd:string,
        "LLMs have shown abili"^^xsd:string,
        "LLMs such as GPT-4"^^xsd:string,
        "Large Language Models Encode Clinical Knowledge"^^xsd:string,
        "Pathways Language Model (PaLM), a dense decoder-only Transformer model, has 540 billion parameters"^^xsd:string,
        "Several studies have shown that LLMs have the capacity to act as implicit knowledge bases"^^xsd:string,
        "The LLM initially generates a preliminary report based on the visual description"^^xsd:string,
        "The trend so far in large language model training has been to increase the model size"^^xsd:string,
        "We propose a method called Clinical Prediction with Large Language Models (CPLLM). This method involves fine-tuning a LLM using prompts"^^xsd:string,
        "We used two different LLMs, Llama2, which is a general LLM (Touvron et al., 2023b) and BioMedLM"^^xsd:string,
        "auto-regressive LLMs are still susceptible to hallucinations and generate erroneous content"^^xsd:string,
        "diverse benchmark to assess the clinical knowledge and question answering capabilities of LLMs"^^xsd:string,
        "enabling us to fully exploit the reasoning capabilities of the LLM in recursively retrieving the most pertinent and valuable knowledge."^^xsd:string,
        "general LLMs typically produce medical advice based solely on their encoded knowledge, without considering specific knowledge in the medical domain"^^xsd:string,
        "highlighting the potential of LLMs in the medical domain"^^xsd:string,
        "large language models face several challenges, including their overwhelming computational requirements"^^xsd:string,
        "large language models should be deployed only with great care, or not at all. Examples include high-stakes domains such as medical diagnoses"^^xsd:string,
        "models ability to generate factual, safe responses to questions that require nuanced answers, typical in real-world medical question-answering."^^xsd:string,
        "resulted LLMs difficult to generalize"^^xsd:string,
        "we fine-tuned two LLMs Llama2 (13B) and BioMedLM (2.7B)"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :medical_classification_model,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "LargeLanguageModel"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A model trained on text data that can be integrated into medical systems but may produce unreliable responses without domain-specific knowledge."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom "CQ_S0_R1_0006"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0033"^^xsd:string,
