    kg:textSpan "increasing number of clusters in different iterations. End-to-end methods such as w2vBERT alleviate the need of coordinating multiple stages. One potential risk for end-to-end approaches compared to k-means clustering is codebook collapse. In w2v-BERT, we nd the contrastive learning objective effectively avoids codebook collapse and thus enables masked prediction training. In addition, unlike other methods that use transformer layers [28] as building blocks, w2v-BERT adopts conformer layers [29]" .

