    kg:textSpan "biomedical domain. While generation methods currently hold great potential, it is important to exercise caution and prudence before deploying them in real-world applications. Further research and development are necessary to refine these models, enhance their accuracy, and establish robust mechanisms for accurateness-checking and error correction. Only through careful scrutiny and continual improvement can we minimize the risks and ethical concerns associated with generation-based medical QA. 6 " .

