    kg:textSpan "model, we use batch size 512 (1M tokens) until step 50k, then double it to 1024 (2M tokens) until step 115k, and nally double again it to 2048 (4M tokens) until training is complete at step 255k. The smaller models followed similar schedules. The reason for using such batch size schedule is twofold: (1) smaller batch sizes are more sample ecient (i.e., better loss as a function of tokens seen) earlier in training, while larger batch sizes are benecial later in training due to better gradient est" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2209_14375_rag__chunk_003> a kg:Chunk ;
