    kg:textSpan ". . . . . . . . . 27 5 Conclusion 27 6 Acknowledgements 27 7 Author contributions 28 Appendix 37 1. Introduction Many deployed machine learning systems operate in settings in which there is no program that computes the systems objective. This is true not only of many natural language tasks, but also of robotics and other tasks where only some aspects of safe behaviour and task completion can be specied a priori. This lack of programmatic reward motivates reinforcement learning from human feedbac" .

