    kg:textSpan "developed to assess competencies of medical students and residents. This exploration consists of a comprehensive evaluation of the performance of GPT-4 on Steps 1-3 of the United States Medical Licensing Examination (USMLE). The exam is part of the ocial accreditation protocol though which medical licensure is determined in the U.S. Our results are based on sample exams and self-assessment materials ocially published by the National Board of Medical Examiners (NBME). The ndings show that zero-sh" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2303_13375_rag__chunk_003> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2303.13375_rag::chunk_003" ;
    kg:docId "2303.13375_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2303_13375_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "we consider six datasets that cover dierent aspects of medical knowledge and reasoning. Two of these datasets, the USMLE Sample Exam and USMLE Self Assessments, are sourced directly from the the National Board of Medical Examiners (NBME), the organization that governs and administers the the examination process. The other four datasets, MedQA, PubMedQA, MedMCQA, and MMLU, are publicly available benchmarks that contain questions based on medical literature, clinical cases, and user-generated cont" .

